e ON clause of the INNER JOIN or as a WHERE clause on a subquery of the respective side. In this case, the original query has multiple joins and filters, but some conditions can be logically associated only with columns from one side of the join. Therefore, these conditions are moved into the ON clause of the INNER JOIN or as a WHERE clause on a subquery of the respective side.\n\nFor example, the condition `cn.country_code ='[us]'` is moved into the ON clause of the first INNER JOIN because it only references columns from one side of the join. Similarly, the condition `rt.role ='costume designer'` is moved into the ON clause of the second INNER JOIN because it also only references columns from one side of the join.\n\nBy applying this query rewrite rule, we can simplify the original query and improve its performance by reducing the number of joins and filters.", 'time': 8.159249305725098}
